<title>HONG KONG: Chi Cheung buys property for HK$160 mln.</title>
<headline>Chi Cheung buys property for HK$160 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Property group Chi Cheung Investment Co Ltd said it had agreed to buy a commercial building from third party Tristan Ltd for HK$160 million.</p>
<p>Chi Cheung said it would fund 40 percent of the purchase by internal resources and 60 percent by bank borrowings.</p>
<p>The property was a 25-storey shop/office building in Arbuthnot Road in the Central district in Hong Kong, with a total gross floor area of 30,949 square feet.</p>
<p>It said it would hold the property for investment purposes and would rent it out on completion of the deal in June.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
